hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15457","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wail, he said: I sat with Shaybah ibn Uthman, so he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sat in this sitting place of yours, so he said: I intended to leave no yellow nor white in the Kabah except I distribute it among the people. He said: I said: That is not for you; your two companions preceded you and did not do that. So he said: They are the two men to be followed."
"15458","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Wasil, from Abu Wail, he said: I sat with Shaybah ibn Uthman in this mosque, so he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sat to me in this sitting place of yours, so he said: I intended to leave in it no yellow nor white except I distribute it among the Muslims. He said: I said: You will not do it. He said: Why? I said: Your two companions did not do it. He said: They are the two men to be followed."
